Loom: pack two 16-bit lanes with one v_perm_b32. vector.from_elements of f16 lanes zero-extended the low half (bfe),
shifted the high half and or-ed them (3 VALU per register), and vector f32 -> f16 truncation zero-extended both halves
and shift-added them (3 VALU). V_PERM_B32 with selector 0x05040100 takes bytes 0..1 of each source whatever their upper
bits, so a pair is one instruction. iu4 gu GEMM epilogue 48 -> 16 packing VALU, f16-output kstore 96 -> 32 per tile.
Bit-identical results.
